In article <CCDI3H.400@tiguex.cs.unm.edu>, mcclure@tiguex.cs.unm.edu (Brent McClure) writes:
>Newsgroups: comp.unix.osf.misc
>From: mcclure@tiguex.cs.unm.edu (Brent McClure)
>Subject: Slow random file access under OSF/1 on Dec alpha
>
>I'm experiencing extremely slow file accesses when I have code that jumps
>around in a file and accesses it at random locations.  The following 
>sample program brings out the problem, and if the output file "foo" is
>large enough ( greater than about 65536 bytes on our system ) then 
>this program runs _much_ slower on our Dec Alpha than on any other
