As an aside:  it is generally a Bad Idea to do any real work inside
a signal handler.  The best way to do things is set a flag which you poll.
Yes, this makes certain problems hard to solve.  It is, however, the most
portable way to do things.

Anyhow, on to your DCE questions:

>      - DCE-RPC is extremely synchronous, therefore, the only way to make it
>        "asynchronous" is to create a thread for each RPC call you send off

