Daniels) writes: 
> I'll give that a shot.  I had gotten the impression that rpc_ep_resolve
> required the directory service...  Isn't the nameservice also part of the
> directory service?  As I said, the problem is that both HP and DEC selll 
> the
> directory service for more than $2000...  Or are you referring to using > 
DNS?
> 

The rpc_ep_* calls talk directly to the rpcd on the server machine, no CDS 
service involved.  Quick clarification: in most cases CDS maps a name to a 
machine (partially bound binding), and that machine's rpcd maps the server 
id to a port (fully bound binding).  Also you can just make the call using 
the partially bound binding (which could have been a string binding) and 
the rpcd will forward it to the right server.

By the way, you might want to check out IBM's prices.  I don't think 
they're near as onerous as what you seem to be hearing from other sources.  
But you do need to distinguish between the security and directory servers 
(you only need one of each per cell) and the client software (which you 
need on each machine and should cost a lot less).

dave



